      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>Indicates that the operation failed because the caller did not have the required permissions. This can occur during resolution, discovery, or callback registration when the caller lacks the <c>android.permission.ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK</c> permission. The failure is reported through <see cref="M:Android.Net.Nsd.NsdManager.IResolveListener.OnResolveFailed(Android.Net.Nsd.NsdServiceInfo,Android.Net.Nsd.NsdFailure)" />, <see cref="M:Android.Net.Nsd.NsdManager.IDiscoveryListener.OnStartDiscoveryFailed(System.String,Android.Net.Nsd.NsdFailure)" />, or <see cref="M:Android.Net.Nsd.NsdManager.IServiceInfoCallback.OnServiceInfoCallbackRegistrationFailed(Android.Net.Nsd.NsdFailure)" />.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/net/nsd/NsdManager#FAILURE_PERMISSION_DENIED" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.net.nsd.NsdManager.FAILURE_PERMISSION_DENIED</code>.</a></format></para>
